4@P0: \nL5@P0: \nL6@P0: \nL7@P0: \nL8@P0: \nL9@P0: \nL10@P0: \nL11@P0: \nL12@P0: \nL13@P0: \nL14@P0: \nL15@P0: \nL16@P0: \nL17@P0: \nL18@P0: \nL19@P0: \nL20@P0: Form Adopted for Mandatory Use IMPORTANT ADVISORY INFORMATION Judicial Council of California\nL21@P0: DAL-001 [Rev. July 1, 2016] FOR BUILDING OWNERS AND TENANTS\nL22@P0: (Disability Access Litigation)\nL23@P0: Civil Code, § 55.3\nL24@P0: www.courts.ca.gov\nL25@P0: Page 1 of 2\nL26@P0: \nL27@P0: \nL28@P0: \nL29@P0: \nL30@P0: \nL31@P0: \nL32@P0: \nL33@P0: \nL34@P0: \nL35@P0: \nL36@P0: \nL37@P0: \nL38@P0: \nL39@P0: \nL40@P0: \nL41@P0: \nL42@P0: \nL43@P0: \nL44@P0: \nL45@P0: \nL46@P0: \nL47@P0: \nL48@P0: \nL49@P0: \nL50@P0: \nL51@P0: \nL52@P0: \nL53@P0: \nL54@P0: \nL55@P0: \nL56@P0: \nL57@P0: \nL58@P0: \nL59@P0: \nL60@P0: \nL61@P0: \nL62@P0: \nL63@P0: \nL64@P0: \nL65@P0: \nL66@P0: \nL67@P0: \nL68@P0: \nL69@P0: \nL70@P0: \nL71@P0: \nL72@P0: \nL73@P0: \nL74@P0: \nL75@P0: \nL76@P0: \nL77@P0: \nL78@P0: \nL79@P0: \nL80@P0: \nL81@P0: \nL82@P0: \nL83@P0: \nL84@P0: \nL85@P0: \nL86@P0: \nL87@P0: \nL88@P0: \nL89@P0: \nL90@P0: \nL91@P0: \nL92@P0: \nL93@P0: \nL94@P0: \nL95@P0: \nL96@P0: \nL97@P0: \nL98@P0: \nL99@P0: \nL100@P0: \nL101@P0: \nL102@P0: \nL103@P0: \nL104@P0: \nL105@P0: \nL106@P0: \nL107@P0: \nL108@P0: \nL109@P0: \nL110@P0: \nL111@P0: \nL112@P0: \nL113@P0: \nL114@P0: \nL115@P0: \nL116@P0: \nL117@P0: \nL118@P0: \nL119@P0: \nL120@P0: \nL121@P0: \nL122@P0: \nL123@P0: \nL124@P0: \nL125@P0: \nL126@P0: \nL127@P0: \nL128@P0: \nL129@P0: DAL-001\nL130@P0: STATE LAW REQUIRES THAT YOU GET THIS IMPORTANT\nL131@P0: ADVISORY INFORMATION FOR BUILDING OWNERS AND TENANTS\nL132@P0: This information is available in English, Spanish, Chinese, Vietnamese, and Korean through the Judicial\nL133@P0: Council of California. People with visual impairments can get assistance in viewing this form through the\nL134@P0: judicial branch website, at www.courts.ca.gov.\nL135@P0: California law requires that you receive this information because the demand letter or court complaint you\nL136@P0: received with this document claims that your building or property does not comply with one or more existing\nL137@P0: construction-related accessibility laws or regulations protecting the civil rights of people with disabilities to\nL138@P0: access public places.\nL139@P0: YOU HAVE IMPORTANT LEGAL OBLIGATIONS. Compliance with disability access laws is a serious\nL140@P0: and significant responsibility that applies to all California building owners and tenants with buildings open for\nL141@P0: business to the public. You may obtain information about your legal obligations and how to comply with\nL142@P0: disability access laws through the Division of the State Architect, at www.dgs.ca.gov/dsa. Information is also\nL143@P0: available from the California Commission on Disability Access at www.ccda.ca.guide.htm.\nL144@P0: YOU HAVE IMPORTANT LEGAL RIGHTS. The allegations made in the accompanying demand letter or\nL145@P0: court complaint do not mean that you are required to pay any money unless and until a court finds you liable.\nL146@P0: Moreover, RECEIPT OF A DEMAND LETTER OR COURT COMPLAINT AND THIS ADVISORY DOES\nL147@P0: NOT NECESSARILY MEAN YOU WILL BE FOUND LIABLE FOR ANYTHING. You will have the right if\nL148@P0: you are later sued to fully present an explanation of why you believe you have not in fact violated disability\nL149@P0: access laws or have corrected the violation or violations giving rise to the claim.\nL150@P0: You have the right to seek assistance or advice about this demand letter or court complaint from any person of\nL151@P0: your choice. If you have insurance, you may also wish to contact your insurance provider. Your best interest\nL152@P0: may be served by seeking legal advice or representation from an attorney, but you may also represent yourself\nL153@P0: and file the necessary court papers to protect your interests if you are served with a court complaint. If you have\nL154@P0: hired an attorney to represent you, you should immediately notify your attorney.\nL155@P0: If a court complaint has been served on you, you will get a separate advisory notice with the complaint advising\nL156@P0: you of special options and procedures available to you under certain conditions.\nL157@P0: ADDITIONAL THINGS YOU SHOULD KNOW: ATTORNEY MISCONDUCT. Except for limited\nL158@P0: circumstances, state law generally requires that a prelitigation demand letter from an attorney MAY NOT\nL159@P0: MAKE A REQUEST OR DEMAND FOR MONEY OR AN OFFER OR AGREEMENT TO ACCEPT\nL160@P0: MONEY. Moreover, a demand letter from an attorney MUST INCLUDE THE ATTORNEY’S STATE BAR\nL161@P0: LICENSE NUMBER.\nL162@P0: If you believe the attorney who provided you with this notice and prelitigation demand letter is not complying\nL163@P0: with state law, you may send a copy of the demand letter you received from the attorney to the State Bar of\nL164@P0: California by facsimile transmission to 1-415-538-2171, or by mail to the State Bar of California, 180 Howard\nL165@P0: Street, San Francisco, CA 94105, Attention: Professional Competence.\nL166@P0: \nL167@P0: \nL168@P0: \nL169@P0: \nL170@P0: \nL171@P0: \nL172@P0: \nL173@P0: \nL174@P0: \nL175@P0: \nL176@P0: \nL177@P0: \nL178@P0: \nL179@P0: STATE LAW REQUIRES THAT YOU GET THIS IMPORTANT\nL180@P0: ADVISORY INFORMATION FOR BUILDING OWNERS AND TENANTS\nL181@P0: \nL182@P0: \nL183@P0: \nL184@P0: \nL185@P0: \nL186@P0: \nL187@P0: \nL188@P0: \nL189@P0: \nL190@P0: \nL191@P0: \nL192@P0: \nL193@P0: \nL194@P0: \nL195@P0: \nL196@P0: \nL197@P0: \nL198@P0: \nL199@P0: \nL200@P0: \nL201@P0: \nL202@P0: \nL203@P0: REDUCING YOUR DAMAGES. If you are a small business owner and correct all of the construction-related\nL204@P0: violations that are the basis of the complaint against you within 30 days of being served with the complaint, you\nL205@P0: may qualify for reduced damages. You may wish to consult an attorney to obtain legal advice. You may also\nL206@P0: wish to contact the California Commission on Disability Access for additional information about the rights and\nL207@P0: obligations of business owners.\nL208@P0: COMMERCIAL TENANT. If you are a commercial tenant, you may not be responsible for ensuring that some\nL209@P0: or all portions of the premises you lease for your business, including common areas such as parking lots, are\nL210@P0: accessible to the public because those areas may be the responsibility of your landlord. You may want to refer\nL211@P0: to your lease agreement and consult with an attorney or contact your landlord, to determine if your landlord is\nL212@P0: responsible for maintaining and improving some or all of the areas you lease.\nL213@P0: DAL-001 [Rev. July 1, 2016] Page 2 of 2 IMPORTANT ADVISORY INFORMATION\nL214@P0: FOR BUILDING OWNERS AND TENANTS\nL215@P0: (Disability Access Litigation)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWG-017/EJ-137 Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/wg017.pdf)\nciteturn1753view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/wg017.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 56\nL0@P0: For your protection and privacy, please press the Clear\nL1@P0: button after you have printed the form.\nL2@P0: Judicial Council of California, courts.ca.gov\nL3@P0: New January 1, 2026, Mandatory Form\nL4@P0: Code Civ. Proc., §§ 684.130, 703.570, 706.105\nL5@P0: Application to Stay Levy or Garnishment\nL6@P0: (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment)\nL7@P0: WG-017/EJ-137\nL8@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL9@P0: LEVYING OFFICER (name and address):\nL10@P0: LEVYING OFFICER FILE NO.:\nL11@P0: COURT CASE NO.:\nL12@P0: ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY: STATE BAR NO.:\nL13@P0: NAME:\nL14@P0: FIRM NAME:\nL15@P0: STREET ADDRESS:\nL16@P0: CITY: STATE: ZIP CODE:\nL17@P0: TELEPHONE NO.: FAX NO.:\nL18@P0: EMAIL ADDRESS:\nL19@P0: ATTORNEY FOR (name):\nL20@P0: SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF\nL21@P0: STREET ADDRESS:\nL22@P0: MAILING ADDRESS:\nL23@P0: CITY AND ZIP CODE:\nL24@P0: BRANCH NAME:\nL25@P0: PLAINTIFF/PETITIONER:\nL26@P0: DEFENDANT/RESPONDENT:\nL27@P0: APPLICATION TO STAY LEVY OR GARNISHMENT\nL28@P0: (Wage Garnishment—Enforcement of Judgment)\nL29@P0: 1.\nL30@P0: asks the court to stay (pause) a wage garnishment, bank account levy, or other levy.\nL31@P0: Judgment debtor (name):\nL32@P0: 2. The judgment debtor received (check all that apply; to list more documents, check here\nL33@P0: a. Notice of Levy (form EJ-150) issued on (date):\nL34@P0: b. Earnings Withholding Order (form WG-002) issued on (date):\nL35@P0: and attach a page\nL36@P0: labeled Attachment 2):\nL37@P0: 3. The levy or garnishment is for a judgment for personal debt.\nL38@P0: (Personal debt means money due or owing because of a transaction for money, property, insurance, or services used primarily for\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1753view7 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc031.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMC-120 Confidential Reference List of Identifiers (https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc120.pdf)\nciteturn1753view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc120.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 57\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1753view9 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.courts.ca.gov/documents/mc356.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn1753view10 